Debian 13 update (2026-10-01)
----------------------------
See QUALIFICATION-DEBIAN13 for the native amd64/arm64 package qualification.
Ubuntu-only scope statements below describe the initial packaging checkpoint.

Debian/Ubuntu packaging for the ncurses module
=============================================

qore-ncurses-module contains the native terminal module, source and compiled
NcursesUi and NcursesReplUi modules, compiler metadata, qrepl and its manual.
qore-ncurses-module-doc contains all three HTML API references and the upstream
test scripts with their shared harness. Debhelper creates matching debug symbols.

Build prerequisites and supported scope
--------------------------------------

Use an isolated native environment with packaged Qore and libqore-dev and all
Build-Depends from debian/control. Current qualification targets Ubuntu 26.04
amd64 with Qore 3.0 development packages. Other Debian/Ubuntu releases and
architectures require their own qualified SDK and native tests. Cross builds
are rejected because Qore tools run during compilation.

The module links distribution wide-character ncurses and panel libraries.
The essential ncurses-base package supplies standard terminal definitions; ncurses-term is recommended
for additional terminal types. Tests use xterm-256color pseudo-terminals and
C.UTF-8, requiring neither a desktop nor an interactive controlling terminal.

The package derives minimum Qore and libqore SONAME dependencies from the SDK
used to build it. dh_shlibdeps supplies other shared-library dependencies.
The runtime package requires the native interpreter and includes shared compiler
metadata, so it is not marked Multi-Arch: same.

AOT modules and documentation
-----------------------------

AOT compilation is enabled, source-tree qmod symlinks are disabled and noopt
selects optimization level zero. The SDK propagates Debian prefix maps into
compiled modules and metadata. Tests explicitly preload the newly built qmods.
Metadata and documentation use the new native/AOT modules and packaged standard
library. CMake honors a caller-supplied QORE_MODULE_DIR_FOR_DOCS and runs final
qdx postprocessing through cmake -E env. This supports isolated builds without
requiring user-installed modules.

The trailer-preservation helper and its real-ELF tests are copied from Qore's
qualified packaging. They preserve dependency/source metadata around dh_strip.
dwz skips this runtime package because it cannot process all LLVM DWARF forms;
dh_strip still creates matching debug symbols for all three ELF modules.

Source and binary builds
------------------------

Use a fresh version for every changed upload. This snapshot precedes 2.0.0.
From a clean committed checkout:

    version=2.0.0~git20260928.1
    mkdir -p ../ncurses-package-work
    git archive --format=tar --prefix="qore-ncurses-module-$version/" \
        HEAD -- . ':!debian' | xz > \
        "../ncurses-package-work/qore-ncurses-module_$version.orig.tar.xz"
    tar -xf "../ncurses-package-work/qore-ncurses-module_$version.orig.tar.xz" \
        -C ../ncurses-package-work
    cp -a debian "../ncurses-package-work/qore-ncurses-module-$version/"
    cd "../ncurses-package-work/qore-ncurses-module-$version"
    dpkg-buildpackage -S -us -uc

Extract the .dsc with dpkg-source -x into a fresh directory. Install dependencies
and run unprivileged with networking disabled:

    dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc

Architecture-only builds (-B) omit documentation and do not need Doxygen.
Architecture-independent builds (-A) produce documentation. The nodoc option
suppresses documentation generation and the nodoc profile omits the doc package.
Do not use nocheck for qualification.

Qualification and publication
-----------------------------

Run all eleven upstream suites. Installed tests copy only the scripts and their
harness to temporary storage, preserving test-relative includes; they explicitly
preload installed qmods with no source-module directory present. They also run
qrepl --help. The compiler fixture creates a pseudo-terminal, draws and reads
text, exercises the input buffer and checks wide-character display width.

The documentation example layout preserves test/TestHarness.qc. To run an
example, change to /usr/share/doc/qore-ncurses-module-doc/examples and invoke
qore test/<suite>.qtest with the runtime package installed.

Check Lintian, hardening/debug links, AOT trailer preservation, runtime-only
install without SDK, documentation/debug coinstallation, dpkg -V, purge/reinstall
and reproducibility from distinct directories. Retain source/package hashes,
dependency inventories and logs. Testing-PPA publication is separate from
approval for a final general release.
